  while `0x003fbed8` is a rewrite; asked for the EXP and the frozen-fixture
  re-pin. Rounds 2–4 caught three classes of typed number: an ad-hoc census
  script that did not mirror `Matcher.verdict` (3369/1319/303 vs the real
  3214/1259/518, and 38 % vs 31.5 %), a stale fixture hash, and "resolved-call
  count 8 vs 7" that was really the call-**sequence** length (both sides have
  11 leaf call sites, 9 distinct callees). Round 5 APPROVE with two negative
  fixture mutations (§ below).
- H85 navigator round 1 found a genuine CI-breaking defect that would have
  shipped: the new CI step captured `tee`'s exit code (`rc=$?` after
  `… | tee gate.txt`), so a FAILing gate exited 0 and the job passed. Fixed
  with `rc=${PIPESTATUS[0]}` (`7b638cf`). It also flagged the SKIP marker set
  being too broad (`cannot verify` would forgive a real verification error);
  the markers were narrowed and a stub pins that exit 2 + `cannot verify` is
  FAIL (selftest 10 → 11 checks). Round 2 APPROVE.

